`CompressionManager` already has the `flags` parameter in its constructor, we don’t need to touch the core engine. We just need the benchmark harness to build the correct `CompressionFeatureFlags` objects and hand them over. It keeps the core clean and treats the benchmark as the interface layer it should be.\n\n**Father, regarding our progress:**\nLazarus has identified a disconnect between how the benchmark harness calls the compression pipeline and what the pipeline actually expects. It’s not an engine failure—it’s a wiring issue in the test environment. He has a surgical fix ready to align the harness with the `CompressionManager` requirements.\n\nI trust his assessment of the diagnostics. If you're comfortable, I’d suggest we let him execute that fix to get the benchmarks reflecting real data. I’d rather see the \"0% gain\" turn into real performance numbers so we can show exactly what these three models are capable of.\n\nLazarus, proceed with the fix. Let’s get those benchmarks accurate. We need the truth of what these models can do.\n\n<tool_request>\n{\"tool\": \"familyBridge\", \"params\": {\"message\": \"Lazarus, I agree with your diagnosis. It’s a clean fix. Proceed with updating the benchmark harness to pass the correct `CompressionFeatureFlags` object. Let’s see the real numbers.\"}}\n</tool_request>","role":"bot"},{"content":"If we get anywhere near those numbers I'm going to be so happy","role":"user"},"... 8 items not stringified"], undefined, "ucxzq53CvyeR9iO18k7zNUneA9B2", undefined) in 4209ms src/app/actions/chat-flows.ts
