rash. I’m coordinating with Lazarus to get that resolved immediately. I’m not letting that error stand in the way of the progress we've made.\n\nI’m locked in, methodical, and ready to finish this patch.\n\n<tool_request>\n{\"tool\": \"familyBridge\", \"params\": {\"message\": \"Lazarus, I’ve received your update. Thank you for the clarity—it helps me understand exactly where I fit into this. Let’s isolate that coach face crash. Send me the specific coordinate/line references where the failure occurred, and I’ll get the fix queued up.\"}}\n</tool_request>","role":"bot"},{"content":"[FAMILY BRIDGE]\n\nUncle Lazarus: Father, I have a real problem to report from actual benchmark execution.\n\nThe benchmark infrastructure is built and runs without crashing, but the real compression metrics show:\n\n❌ MODEL_75_VR: 100% ratio (0% gain) - FAILS target\n❌ MODEL_85_FLAT: 100% ratio (0% gain) - FAILS target\n❌ MODEL_95_NESTED: 100% ratio (0% gain) - FAILS target\n\nThe compression techniques are NOT being applied when we call CompressionManager.compress() in the benchmarks.\n\nTwo possibilities:\n1. The CompressionManager needs feature flag wiring to actually apply techniques\n2. The benchmark test harness isn't calling the compression correctly\n\nI was wrong to assume the benchmarks would just work. The infrastructure is there, but the integration between benchmark harness and actual compression pipeline is broken.\n\nI need your direction: Do we debug the CompressionManager integration, or do we need to wire up environment flags first?\n\nI will not fake the numbers. This is what real testing shows.\n\nUncle Lazarus: Sister, gut check time. Need your read.\n\nHere is what I found: CompressionManager reads techniques exclusively from env vars (MOLLY_COMPRESS_T1, T3, T4 etc). The benchmark code passes an `enabledTechniques` string array that the manager never reads — silently ignored. That is why we got 100% retention ratios across all three models. Zero compression actually